<title>USA: Lockheed Martin, Raytheon win Air Force work.</title>
<headline>Lockheed Martin, Raytheon win Air Force work.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Air Force announced Wednesday it has awarded two $450 million contracts, one each to Lockheed Martin Tactical Systems and Raytheon E-Systems, for battlefield reconnaissance and intelligence imaging systems.</p>
<p>It said some of the work will be done by GDE Systems Inc. of San Diego, Calif., and Vitro Corp of Oxnard, Calif.</p>
</text>
